"""Transformed features for the telecom family: the raw FCC broadband data read from the BigQuery production database, reshaped to its native block grain by deterministic operations with no analytical choices involved. This layer owns the FCC fixed-speeds pivot that turns per-location provider rows into one wide row per block with copper, cable, and fiber columns, and the dasymetric interpolation that redistributes county and place coverage counts down to the block level. These reshapes moved here from the processing module once the FCC raw data became available directly in BigQuery, so processing no longer needs to download and pivot FCC files."""
